FC-08 — Company & User-Company Relationship Management

Version: 3.2.2
Status: Implementation-Ready / TDD-Ready
Type: Feature Contract / Intermediate Architecture & Implementation Specification
Domain: Company / User-Company Relationship
Depends on: FC-05, FC-06, FC-07
Author: Senior Product Architect + CTO
Date: 30 August 2026

1. Purpose

FC-08 establishes the foundational domain model for Company and the relationship between a User and a Company.

The feature allows a User to:

create and manage Companies;
associate themselves with one or more Companies;
act under different contextual roles for different Companies;
hold multiple roles for the same Company;
archive a Company or User-Company relationship without physically deleting the data;
provide the legal and administrative context required by future Foresy features.

FC-08 deliberately does not implement accounting, fiscal calculation, forecasting, simulation, CRA evolution, or regulatory calculation engines.

It establishes the structural foundation required for those future capabilities.

2. Product Context

Foresy is a backend-first SaaS product for independent professionals.

Its purpose is to help users:

manage their professional activity;
accurately track work;
understand their legal and fiscal situation;
simulate the consequences of business decisions;
plan future activity;
gain visibility over their activity over time.

The frontend is out of scope.

FC-08 is therefore concerned exclusively with backend:

domain modeling;
persistence;
relationships;
REST APIs;
validation;
authorization;
testing;
Swagger/OpenAPI documentation.
