Given an authenticated User
When the User creates a Company with an invalid SIREN
Then the request fails
And the Company is not created
And no UserCompany relationship is created
Scenario 8 — Duplicate SIREN
Given a Company with a given SIREN already exists
When a User attempts to create another Company with the same SIREN
Then the request fails
And no duplicate Company is created
Scenario 9 — SIRET Absent
Given an authenticated User
When the User creates a Company without a SIRET
Then the Company is created
And the SIRET is NULL
Scenario 10 — Duplicate SIRET
Given a Company with a given SIRET already exists
When a User attempts to create another Company with the same SIRET
Then the request fails
And no duplicate Company is created
Scenario 11 — Atomicity
Given an authenticated User
When Company creation succeeds
And UserCompany creation fails
Then the transaction is rolled back
And the Company does not exist
And the UserCompany relationship does not exist
