64. Final Architectural Position

FC-08 establishes the following canonical model:

                         ┌────────────────────┐
                         │        User        │
                         └─────────┬──────────┘
                                   │
                                   │
                         ┌─────────▼──────────┐
                         │    UserCompany     │
                         │                    │
                         │ user_id            │
                         │ company_id         │
                         │ role               │
                         │ deleted_at         │
                         └─────────┬──────────┘
                                   │
                                   │
                         ┌─────────▼──────────┐
                         │      Company       │
                         │                    │
                         │ name               │
                         │ siren              │
                         │ siret              │
                         │ legal_form         │
                         │ vat_regime         │
                         │ address...          │
                         │ country            │
                         │ currency           │
                         │ deleted_at         │
                         └────────────────────┘

The resulting architectural rule is:

A User does not belong to a Company. A User acts in a contextual role in relation to a Company.

This distinction is foundational for Foresy's future ability to represent:

User
 ├── Company A → independent
 │       └── Missions / CRA / activity
 │
 └── Company B → client
         └── Projects / Missions / external independents

It also allows:

User
 └── Company A
       ├── independent
       └── client

without conflating the underlying business contexts.

FC-08 therefore establishes the Company and contextual relationship foundation without prematurely introducing the fiscal, regulatory, forecasting, simulation, or accounting engines that will consume this foundation in future Feature Contracts.

